libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; color: rgb(=
0, 0, 0); margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 5px;">
Rotation owners (continued)</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 15px;">
<b>Q13.</b> UserMaintenance owner: <code>FIS_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> / <code>co=
m.fis.encryption.key</code> (f001) and re-encryption of the blobs it protects=
.</div>

<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; color: rgb(=
0, 0, 0); margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 5px;">
Vault integration (new)</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 5px;">
<b>Q14.</b> Vault admin: which Vault namespace and KV mount should IBSMAS use=
 per tier, and who creates the bic-sso secret path (<code>secret/ibsmas/&lt;t=
ier&gt;/dwbo-bic-sso/bo4-trusted-auth</code>), its read-only policy, and the =
Vault Proxy AppRole for each tier?
<ul style=3D"margin: 3px 0 8px 25px; padding: 0;">
  <li>Needed before f010 can be deployed to SYSTEM.</li>
  <li>The mount must be a KV version 2 engine. Both the current Snowflake cli=
ent (VaultSharp) and the new Vault client read KV v2 only (latest version, vi=
a <code>&lt;mount&gt;/data/&lt;path&gt;</code>), and neither works against a =
KV v1 mount.</li>
  <li>Is the mount named <code>kv</code> or <code>secret</code>? The current =
Snowflake client's code defaults to <code>kv</code>, but its config requires =
the mount to be set explicitly, while the new client and the proposed path <c=
ode>secret/ibsmas/&lt;tier&gt;/...</code> assume <code>secret</code>. A copy =
of the <code>kvMountPoint</code> and <code>vaultNamespace</code> values from =
a deployed Snowflake-client config would settle it, as would <code>vault secr=
ets list -detailed</code> in each tier's namespace.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 5px;">
<b>Q15.</b> Operations: who rotates the Vault Proxy secret_id on each bic-sso=
 Tomcat host, and is its expiry monitored?
<ul style=3D"margin: 3px 0 8px 25px; padding: 0;">
  <li>It is reusable, ACL'd to the Proxy service account, bound to the server=
 CIDRs, and expires after 90 days. An expired secret_id does not stop a runni=
ng Proxy (its periodic token keeps renewing). SSO fails only at the next Prox=
y restart or host reboot, so the failure can stay hidden until a patch-night =
reboot. Monitor the secret_id's own expiry, not the Proxy or its token.</li>
  <li>For SYSTEM testing of expiry, can the Vault admin revoke a test secret_=
id, or mint one with a short TTL, rather than waiting 90 days?</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 5px;">
<b>Q16.</b> BOE admin: when can the trusted-authentication shared secret be r=
otated in the CMC and Vault together?
<ul style=3D"margin: 3px 0 8px 25px; padding: 0;">
  <li>The current value is protected only by a key that is still in git histo=
ry, so it must be rotated before Readiness and Production.</li>
  <li>The application caches the value for up to 5 minutes, so expect up to 5=
 minutes of failed SSO logins after cutover unless Tomcat is restarted.</li>
  <li>Does the CMC keep accepting the old secret during the transition?</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 5px;">
<b>Q17.</b> Network/Security: is there any proxy, NAT, or load balancer betwe=
en the application hosts and Vault?
<ul style=3D"margin: 3px 0 8px 25px; padding: 0;">
  <li>AppRole tokens and secret_ids are bound to the server CIDRs, so a rewri=
tten source IP would break login and renewal.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 5px;">
<b>Q18.</b> Operations: on Linux hosts, who delivers a new wrapped secret_id =
to the Vault Proxy after each restart or reboot? Or should Linux use the same=
 persistent-file model as Windows?</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 5px;">
<b>Q19.</b> Pipeline: how do Jenkins and Azure DevOps authenticate to Vault (=
JWT/OIDC, or a separate AppRole) to mint wrapped secret_ids?
<ul style=3D"margin: 3px 0 8px 25px; padding: 0;">
  <li>Is it acceptable for the Azure deployment job to mint the secret_id on =
the same VM that consumes it?</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 15px;">
<b>Q20.</b> Pipeline/JFrog: is <code>com.fisglobal:fis-mvn-parent:1.1.1</code=
> the right parent and JFrog target for publishing the shared Vault client li=
brary (<code>com.fis.foundation.vault:vault-client:0.1.0</code>), and who has=
 deploy rights?</div>

<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-to=
p: 15px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
A decision on <b>Q1</b>, <b>Q4</b>, <b>Q7=E2=80=93Q9</b>, and <b>Q14</b> unbl=
ocks production deployment of f006, f010, f012, f014, and f001.</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 5px;">
Thanks,</div>
<div style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_EmbeddedFont, Aptos_MSFontService, Ca=
libri, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); margin-bo=
ttom: 15px;">
Joe</div>
